  "findings": [
    "The previous final-image comparisons omitted non-neutral output grading. The observed, unfitted grading approximation reduces baseline mean RGB error by about 44% in both new stem views.",
    "Correcting this omission reverses the relative result for several first-block variants: graded branch-rounding, direct-MMA and native-activation diagnostics improve over their graded baseline on the exactly paired contract image.",
    "Native first-block activation substitutions are still not independent models; none of the reconstructions matches the native output.",
    "No native latency improvement was measured; the output-grade comparisons run on CPU and do not execute a neural model."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "One scene and first-reset comparisons, not cross-scene or temporal validation.",
    "Parameter observation is from one view; reuse on other paired captures is explicitly an inference from the same runtime, controls and reset state.",
    "Algebraic HSL simplification and omitted neutral special-function rounding mean the output stage is not bit exact.",
    "No binaries, weights, images, textures, tensors, disassembly, private paths or device addresses are published."
